  "limitations": [
    "This is the first bounded workflow trial, not a compiler rewrite, cold compiler optimization, complete integration pass, installed promotion, independent reconstruction or whole-product qualification. No release scope was reduced.",
    "The prepared-only path can still compile/package missing target products, bounded by the selected total deadline. A missing compiler checkpoint is an incomplete development prerequisite, never passing evidence. Existing default construction-enabled CLI and automatic verification routing remain unchanged.",
    "The cache owner uses controlled producers for acquisition and failure tests. The real CLI miss uses an empty private cache. A complete current-source integration run with a populated exact current compiler checkpoint was not run; retained products support the separate runtime timing sample.",
    "One final timing sample per host on the same physical machine, with overlapping host runs and WSL repository access. No isolated performance threshold or peak-memory claim. Windows and Debian Node versions differ and are recorded per run.",
    "The earlier 249678 ms source build and 20-second package precheck are historical local diagnostic logs. All-function inspection can reject that known native bound early; it does not replace verification or native lowering on accepted inputs.",
    "Windows replacement-race testing exposed imprecise numeric file identifiers. Work-directory identity now uses bigint stat fields; the existing directory replacement case passes. An initial Windows run failed its replacement-case command-count assertion before this correction.",
    "A temporary measurement wrapper initially expected the wrong runtime summary string; the underlying Debian runtime owner passed. The wrapper was corrected before the recorded final measurements.",
    "Broader compiler/runtime/source suites were not run for these JavaScript workflow changes. The full changed-file plan also includes unfinished feature changes and was deliberately not executed."
